 examples?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:fff6a7782b613baac41e699dabffd995958cf249265239c921f2d9ad3646f9dc","title":"Can classical type IIB compactifications with O5/O7-planes generate potentials for all geometric moduli, stabilize them in controlled vacua, and admit metastable de Sitter vacua or slow-roll inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:fffe9d4451f96329fa33ba038d7b5572a01e35bc98cfb828ac9b00c74d2f413c","title":"Could relativistic axionic dark radiation convert in the Milky Way magnetic field strongly enough to explain ROSAT soft X-ray backgrounds or emission above and below the Galactic centre, and which axion parameters would overproduce those signals?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff0b554e013896bfb18f6179fa53f15a82935ed41532c051a45db7541da2e4bb","title":"Which charged matter representations and spectra arise from singular gauge divisors in elliptic F-theory compactifications? The principal setting is a complex surface base giving 6D supergravity, with global examples on P² and a stated extension to non-chiral 4D models.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0025"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff6fee2e22c26355b23101209115b88cedb4816425583a99ea5156885e61a4f3","title":"How can topological-string calculations provide quantities in a four-dimensional supersymmetric field theory after gravitational modes are decoupled?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff94d1acd48ad3f2ea9ae25e67a77b9ef2af77a094be18bb94c8d0d5832ba6cb","title":"Can periodic modulations and gauge-particle production in axion monodromy inflation 