"},{"id":"source-question:fff3199b766afdd2bb2bdbb87d3ba8ffd57e6aa5385bc1a5544530bb510800f2","title":"What can the shape of a positive multifield potential constrain without specifying cosmological initial conditions? The paper studies gradient, tachyon and finite-distance descent diagnostics, with lengths measured using the scalar kinetic metric.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff3a148c17a430bd237d023cb66bb70efdfd565d4b83e100210e9c5296e4dbe1","title":"Can a nonsymmetric model enter hyperinflation after an initially stable slow-roll phase? Here negative curvature destabilises the transverse direction as the quadratic potential becomes relatively steeper during descent.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff6e5c9f362ef2405a4c290978ce050944e9987a99ee38ce1ae9521bb42b2327","title":"Does corrected T-duality preserve non-extremal black-hole horizons, entropy and temperature throughout a two-parameter family of four-derivative theories, including parameter choices without a known string-theory origin?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff4df8cb3ced079f9e0481751aa6a754ed276970403cd3c12448541e4cee3a9f","title":"The local potential family tests whether inflation can persist near a maximum or inflection point while quantum kicks compete with outward classical drift. The retained quadratic term matters for satisfying a finite tachyonic-curvature requirement.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ffc295e02ea2bc590df9ee37dbbe4706bec8ab5d89587f1d6e2f90a8748b3c87","title":"Can quantum extremal surfaces and entanglement wedge reconstruction explain the Page curve, information recovery and a smooth evaporating horizon while retaining semiclassical Hawking entanglement? How does recovery depend on knowledge of the initial state?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff76587d6ae11c6d8219196e85f05201f4bbc9111a85642fd6331548906d1a8e","title":"Do boundary-driven Einstein–Born–Infeld solutions in AdS provide counterexamples to weak cosmic censorship, and can a sufficiently charged scalar remove them? How do the inferred charge thresholds depend on the Born–Infeld parameter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff1416eab4447be83f73a0670413dc5936395308fdbe3eff075a982db6858167","title":"How do higher-curvature corrections in the EFT of GR change gravitational-wave propagation relative to minimally coupled matter on backgrounds that spontaneously break Lorentz invariance, and what can positivity and causality imply about the sign?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff00b93ebedd5a951d245f6659f7f55cecdb8cbd445970d64fb214e83970c176","title":"What foundational, mathematical, physical, and quantum problems remain open in theoretical cosmology, particularly concerning cosmological assumptions, inflation, nonlinear structure, averaging, singularities, and quantum gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff40e35ea70a2b50f4bd9d18fbaef504bfb4d2b422d74573d34128670dfb2b8c","title":"Which spin backgrounds remain allowed after including the heterotic B-field constraint? The distinction depends on Yang–Mills flux and fivebrane sources.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ff07ef3ceaea434a36ce7a73250261e4b0f8a0082eba724